menu "Buttons (drivers/buttons)"

    config BUTTONS_MAX
        int "Maximum buttons per configuration"
        default 4
        range 1 16
        help
            Size of the static per-button state table (ADR-005). buttons_init()
            rejects a configuration with more entries than this.

    config BUTTONS_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Default debounce time (ms)"
        default 20
        range 1 500
        help
            A level must be stable for this long before it is accepted as a press
            or release. Mechanical switches settle in 1-20 ms; raise it for a
            noisy switch, lower it for a tactile dome if latency matters.

    config BUTTONS_LONG_PRESS_MS
        int "Default long-press threshold (ms)"
        default 800
        range 100 10000
        help
            A press held this long emits BUTTONS_EVENT_LONG_PRESS once. The
            application decides what a long press means (ADR-013).

    config BUTTONS_REPEAT_MS
        int "Default auto-repeat period after a long press (ms)"
        default 200
        range 20 5000
        help
            While a button stays held past the long-press threshold and the
            configuration enables auto_repeat, BUTTONS_EVENT_REPEAT fires every
            this many milliseconds (volume-style hold).

    config BUTTONS_SAMPLE_MS
        int "Sampling period while any button is active (ms)"
        default 5
        range 1 50
        help
            After an edge interrupt the task samples every pin at this period until
            all buttons are released and settled, then blocks again. Sets the
            resolution of every timing above; must be well under DEBOUNCE_MS.

    config BUTTONS_IDLE_POLL_MS
        int "Idle wake-up period (ms)"
        default 1000
        range 100 30000
        help
            While idle the task still wakes at this period to re-sample the pins
            and feed the watchdog, so a missed edge interrupt (e.g. across a sleep
            transition) is recovered within one period. Must be below the task
            watchdog timeout (DIAG_WDT_TIMEOUT_S).

    config BUTTONS_TASK_PRIORITY
        int "Button task priority"
        default 8
        range 1 10
        help
            Human-timescale work: below every SDK deadline task (SDD §8.1). The
            application's event callback runs at this priority, on this task.

    config BUTTONS_TASK_CORE
        int "Button task core affinity"
        default 0
        range 0 1
        help
            Core 0, away from the audio deadline tasks on core 1 (ADR-009).

    config BUTTONS_TASK_STACK
        int "Button task stack (bytes)"
        default 3072
        range 2048 16384
        help
            The application's callback runs on this stack; raise it if the
            callback does more than hand the event on.

endmenu
